<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The recording ring: an unfilled circle drawn BEHIND the bubble, scaled and
  faded by BubbleService from the live microphone level.

  @color/dicta_live rather than @color/dicta_accent, and that is the point of
  having a second token at all — the accent is the dictation *affordance* (the
  bubble's own ring, the mic pill, a focused field), so a pulse in the accent
  would read as "this button is emphasised" rather than "you are being
  recorded". dicta_live is reserved for the live state and is measured at
  5.67:1 on surface_2.

  🔴 It is never the only signal. The bubble's contentDescription changes with
  the state (@string/bubble_recording) and a labelled cancel button appears
  beneath it, because a pulsing hue on its own is a colour-and-motion-only
  state indicator — see the "State is never carried by colour alone" section
  in res/values/colors.xml.

  Unfilled: the bubble sits on top of this at full opacity, so a solid fill
  would be invisible under it and would only show as a hard edge where it grows
  past the bubble's rim.
-->
<shape xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:shape="oval">
    <solid android:color="@android:color/transparent" />
    <stroke
        android:width="3dp"
        android:color="@color/dicta_live" />
</shape>
